<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Prussian Academy of Sciences</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1700">1700</a>–<a href="/years/1945">1945</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as Berlin Academy</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Prussian Academy of Sciences was founded in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berlin">Berlin</a> in 1700 by Elector <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-i-of-prussia">Frederick III of Brandenburg</a> on the advice of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gottfried-wilhelm-leibniz">Gottfried Wilhelm Leibniz</a>, its first president. It became one of the leading learned societies of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dimitrie-cantemir">Dimitrie Cantemir</a> of Moldavia was elected a member in 1714.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/prussian-academy-of-sciences.jpg" alt="Prussian Academy of Sciences" width="320" height="453" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Andreas Praefcke · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Berlin_Stabi_UdL_Eingang_Preussische_Akademie_der_Wissenschaften.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
